{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"duration","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP8DurationQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP8DurationQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"customError","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")? = nil) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncSequences","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Timeout","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Timeout","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Clock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"name":"duration","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The longest the sequence may go without an element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"clock","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The clock that measures the gaps."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"tolerance","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tolerance of the timer’s sleeps. Defaults to "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"customError","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The error to throw when the timer fires. Defaults to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeoutError.timedOut(duration:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"anchor":"return-value","level":2,"text":"Return Value","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sequence of the same elements that throws if the upstream goes quiet."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timer starts when iteration begins and restarts with every element, so it bounds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wait for the first element and each gap after it, never the sequence as a whole. Elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass through unchanged. When the timer fires, the upstream is cancelled and the sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws, without waiting for the upstream to respond to the cancellation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and elements it produces while the consumer is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"busy are buffered, so the timer measures the upstream’s gaps. A duration of zero or less","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws before the first element.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Example","level":2,"text":"Example"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let clock = ContinuousClock()","for try await line in bytes.lines.timeout(.seconds(30), clock: clock) {","    handle(line)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"TimeoutError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"code":"customError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") when ","type":"text"},{"code":"duration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" passes between elements, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any error the upstream throws.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Throws","style":"note"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On WASI, a sleep on a real clock ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContinuousClock"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuspendingClock"},{"type":"text","text":") holds the one thread"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"until its deadline, even when other work is ready, and cancelling it doesn’t end it sooner. So the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timer can hold the thread before the upstream runs, then count that wait against it and throw even"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"though elements were ready. A test clock is unaffected."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Afluent","relatedModules":["_Concurrency"]}],"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"timeout"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP8DurationQa","kind":"